<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Intendancy of Guadalajara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1786–1821</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Intendancy of Guadalajara was an administrative division of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a> created in 1786 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bourbon-reforms">Bourbon Reforms</a>, which replaced the older kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-galicia">New Galicia</a> with intendancies run by royal officials. Governed from Guadalajara, it covered roughly the modern states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalisco">Jalisco</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayarit">Nayarit</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aguascalientes">Aguascalientes</a> and Colima. It lasted until Mexican independence in 1821, when it became the province and then the state of Jalisco.</p></div>
